<!--BlockML Documentation — update A02 page skeletons
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task.A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons-->
<task:A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that updates A02 page skeletons
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A02 structuring task: PagePlan.scope names the topic only.

    - **Sources** — read this task's authorativeSources and select the SSOT
      Blocks that cover each page's scope. Write a page-local
      authoritativeSources set that tightens that task set — never copy
      BlockMLSourceSet wholesale
    - **Planning fields** — map PagePlan.scope, readerOutcome,
      learningObjective, exclusion, and supportingPoint onto the page
      aggregations scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives, exclusions,
      and supportingPoints. Refine each from the plan and the bound sources
    - **Skeleton** — write a formulated purpose plus see links to those sources
    - **Overwrite** — an existing skeleton is replaced; its content is never
      used as input
    - **Body** — page body content stays for a03
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          PagePlan carries name plus five Text planning fields. scope is what
          the page covers — not a purpose, title, or outline. readerOutcome,
          learningObjective, exclusion, and supportingPoint refine the
          intent. Structuring must open this task's authorativeSources, choose
          the SSOT Blocks that cover scope, write a page-local source set that
          tightens the task set, map the five planning fields onto Page
          aggregations (refined, not copied), and write a formulated purpose
          from what those Blocks actually say.

          1. Read the plan
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan. Walk every nested
          PagePlan under rootPageGroupPlan. Ignore PageGroupPlan entries. For each
          PagePlan collect name plus the five Text fields: scope, readerOutcome,
          learningObjective, exclusion, supportingPoint. BmlDocSetPlan has no
          authoritativeSources; sources come from this task.

          2. Open the authoritative sources before writing a page
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type for each
          selector on org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source.BlockMLSourceSet). That
          set is the whitelist this task may draw domain content from. For each
          candidate, inspect is, documentation, and references — do not guess
          from the FQN or from scope alone.

          3. Bind sources to scope and write a page-local source set
          For each PagePlan, select the source Blocks whose documented subject
          matches that page's scope. Those selected Blocks are the page's
          authoritative sources. Every content page must have at least one
          Requires source from the whitelist. If several sources match,
          Requires = primary SSOT for the scope; SeeAlso = supporting
          background. Do not attach a source that does not serve the scope.

          Do not copy this task's authorativeSources onto the page. Do not
          compose source:BlockMLSourceSet on the page, and do not reuse its
          package-wildcard includedTypes (org.blockml.bml.core.** and siblings).
          Create an individual workflow:AuthorativeSourceSet for that page
          whose includedTypes are a tightening of the task set: exact
          TypeSelectors (FQNs) of the bound SSOT Blocks only. Every selector
          must match the task whitelist and none of its blacklist. Two pages
          share the same includedTypes only when their scopes actually bind
          the same Blocks. Structural templates (docgen page elements, sector
          Blocks) may appear as see-links; they must not appear in
          includedTypes.

          Write that set on Page.authoritativeSources as owned
          AuthorativeSourceSet instances (override="true", composition), not
          as a type reference to BlockMLSourceSet. Index / menu pages still
          get a page-local set; if no whitelist Block covers that page's
          scope, includedTypes may be empty, but see-links to structural
          templates remain.

          4. Formulate the skeleton from the plan and the bound sources
          The a02 subpackages data, page, and pagegroup
          (org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup) are created
          by A02_01_UpdateDocSet if they do not already exist. This task does not
          create those packages.

          Resolve the A02 FQN as
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page + "." + PagePlan.name
          (for example docs.FirstBlock →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.FirstBlock).
          Do not write in page packages of other sectors — only this a02
          page package, never a page package outside a02 (a03 or any later
          sector). Do not create or edit pages outside a02, PageGroups,
          or pageMapping.

          If a skeleton with that name already exists, discard its current content
          and regenerate the file from the plan and the bound authoritative sources.
          Existing skeleton content is never authoritative: do not treat it as true,
          and do not use it as input for generation (not is, documentation, purpose,
          title, see links, authoritativeSources, semantic aggregations, or any
          other field). Keep only the FQN / file path so the same Block is
          overwritten. Do not invent pages that are not in the plan.

          Write purpose as a finished renderer instruction: why this page exists and
          what it must accomplish, grounded in the bound sources (their is /
          documentation / claims). Do not copy scope into purpose and do not leave
          purpose as a topic list.

          Map the five PagePlan Text properties onto Page aggregations as owned
          semantic instances. Inspect org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.Page,
          org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.SemanticAnnotation, and
          org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.* for member shape. Inspect
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03 only
          for how page-level authoritativeSources and the five semantic lists
          are filled — never copy its domain claims or its content tree.

          Each planning field becomes one or more owned instances. summary is a
          refined formulation of the plan text, grounded in what the bound
          sources actually say — not a verbatim copy of the PagePlan attribute.
          Split into several instances when the plan text contains distinct
          claims. Tighten wording against the bound sources (names, distinctions,
          bounds those Blocks actually document). Do not invent claims the plan
          and sources do not support. Do not drop a planning field that the
          PagePlan set. Index / menu pages still get all five aggregations.

          Mapping (PagePlan Text property → Page aggregation / instance type):
          - scope → scopes (org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.Scope)
          - readerOutcome → readerOutcomes (org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.ReaderOutcome)
          - learningObjective → learningObjectives (org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.LearningObjective)
          - exclusion → exclusions (org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.Exclusion);
            set reason when the plan or bound sources explain why the topic
            is omitted
          - supportingPoint → supportingPoints (org.blockml.bml.docgen.semantic.SupportingPoint)

          On each semantic instance, authoritativeSources may further tighten
          the page set to the Blocks that ground that claim. Do not expand
          beyond the page set. Omit LearningObjective.priority and
          prerequisites unless the plan clearly implies them.

          Each skeleton must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.DocPage
            (not org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.Page)
          - set is to one short identity sentence informed by the bound sources
          - set documentation to name the scope, name the bound source FQNs, and
            state that body content is authored in a03 from those sources
          - override title, purpose, detailLevel (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*),
            and pageType (org.blockml.bml.docgen.pagetype.*) from the bound sources
          - list each bound source as references/see (Requires or SeeAlso)
          - fill authoritativeSources with the page-local AuthorativeSourceSet
            from step 3
          - fill scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives, exclusions, and
            supportingPoints from the PagePlan fields as refined in this step
          - omit DocPage.content and Page.rules / audiences. Do not author
            sections, paragraphs, or other page body
          - omit docset

          5. Register every A02 page on BmlDocSet_A02
          Update org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.BmlDocSet_A02.
          Put every A02 skeleton written in this task into BmlDocSet_A02.pages
          (TypeReferenceEntity links, plan order). Do not invent pages that are
          not in the plan.

          Set BmlDocSet_A02.homePage from BmlDocSetPlan.homePage, resolved to
          the matching A02 page FQN (a02 page package + the planned page name,
          for example docs.TableOfContents →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.TableOfContents).
          homePage must be one of the a02 pages in pages.

          BmlDocSet_A02.pages and homePage may contain only a02 pages. Never
          insert or keep a page from another sector (a03 or later). If an
          existing pages entry is outside a02, remove it. Do not edit DocSets
          of other sectors.

          Export each A02 skeleton from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not
          already in the catalog. Do not remove a03 catalog entries.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons>
